vpinos-core (1.1.16) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Live USB: when settings can't be saved because the USB stick was
    written in ISO (file-copy) mode -- Rufus's default -- the main menu
    and System Info now say so, and to write the ISO again in DD mode
    (Rufus's "DD Image" mode, balenaEtcher, or dd). Before, they only
    said the stick wasn't laid out as expected.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:11:07 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.15) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Live USB: settings can now be saved on the USB stick. Pick the
    "save settings to USB" entry at the boot menu (VPinOS 1.1.5 ISO or
    newer). The first time, VPinOS makes a partition in the free space
    after the image -- all of it, if there's at least 1 GB -- and from
    then on your VPinOS Configuration, VPinball and VPinFE settings,
    tables, Wi-Fi and Boot on startup are kept. Pick the same entry
    every time; the normal entry starts without them.
  * The main menu on a live session says whether settings are being
    saved, and System Info shows it under Session.
  * Setup > Boot on startup is also offered on a live USB that saves its
    settings.
  * New: Tools > Reset Saved Settings (live USB with saved settings)
    clears them and reboots.
  * Not saved: anything installed (VR components, VPX Editor, updates).
    Writing the ISO to the stick again removes the saved settings.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:57:17 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.14) trixie; urgency=medium

  * VPinOS Configuration: the sound output profile picked under Sound
    Output is now remembered after a reboot. Before, the sound switched
    straight away but went back to the default at the next login, and
    the page showed the default again. Pick your sound output once more
    after updating.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:12:21 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.13) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New menu: the VPinOS menu is now a full-screen menu with the logo,
    version and IP at the top. Move with the arrow keys and Enter, or
    press the same number and letter keys as before; Esc or q goes back,
    and every submenu has a Back item for cabinets with only a joystick
    and buttons. The highlighted item is described under the list, and
    settings show their current value next to them.
  * Console Rotation, GPU Driver, Boot on startup and SSH Password
    Authentication open a list of choices with the current one marked.
    Shutdown and Reboot ask Yes/No.
  * The old text menu is still there and comes up if the new one can't
    run (the console fallback when kmscon fails).

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:46:45 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.12) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The console the menu runs in is now kmscon instead of the kernel's
    text console, so text is drawn with real fonts and full Unicode and
    colour work. Takes effect at the next reboot after updating. If
    kmscon can't start, the old console and menu come up instead.
  * Console Rotation now applies to kmscon too: changing it restarts the
    console, already rotated, without a reboot. On a multi-screen
    cabinet the menu only shows on the largest screen.
  * Changing the GPU Driver now switches straight away (the console
    restarts) instead of on the next launch.
  * Needs vpinos-platform 1.0.3, which adds kmscon to the backports
    packages VPinOS follows.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:22:20 -0500

